Changes: English labels, one-line layout, merged with the usage gauges below.

This copy is adapted from plugins/token-weather-usage 3.10.7 of
https://github.com/augiefra/claude-mods (Apache License, Version 2.0) by
anderson-spider. Changes from that version: English only (the French labels and
the language option are gone); the limits' bars are block characters in the
terminal and the app, without the percentage while a bar is shown; a mark and
the gap in points against the clock beside each limit (▲ ahead, ▼ behind,
▬ on pace) and the Pace start option; the cache shows its time left with the
x1.25 write multiplier for the 5-minute lifetime, the yellow threshold follows
the lifetime, and dollar amounts only appear with the Show cost option.

The 5-hour and 7-day usage gauges were written for this mod after
usage-meter by HolyGrail (https://github.com/HolyGrail/claude-mods/tree/main/plugins/usage-meter):
same idea (gauges with an elapsed-time marker, a reading shared across
sessions), without copying its code.

The prompt cache block (share of the prompt read from the cache, time left
before it lapses, missed and expired states) was written for this mod after
prompt-cache-control by Daniel San (https://github.com/davila7/claude-code-templates,
MIT): same idea (cache usage per request, an inferred lifetime and a
countdown), without copying its code.
